<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 30,477,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 30,477,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 02/12/97    02/05/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 30,477,000  30,537,000    26,140,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	 162,403     163,663	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	35,324,000  35,324,000    33,981,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,516,775  35,516,775	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   02/12/97    02/05/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   4,879,000   5,434,000     4,434,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    5,108,000   5,286,000     4,346,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  5,158,000   5,015,000     4,601,000</p>
<p> South Central    3,327,000   3,105,000     2,538,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  4,221,000   4,268,000     3,332,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 5,484,000   5,456,000     4,906,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  2,300,000   1,973,000     1,983,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	30,477,000  30,537,000    26,140,000</p>
